<h2>Segment 219 &mdash; the dormant seeds during direct perception</h2>
<div class="pair">
<div class="tib"><div class="lab">TIBETAN (WYLIE)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s219S">&#x27;o na <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w1"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s219w2">mthong</span> lam</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w3">bar chad med lam</span> gyi <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w4">dus</span> su de&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w5">spang bya</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w6">mthong spang</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w7">med</span> mod kyang , <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w8">sgom spang</span> gi <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w9">bag la nyal</span> yod dgos la, <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s219w10">de&#x27;i tshe</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w11"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s219w12">yid</span> kyi <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s219w13">shes pa</span></span> ni <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s219p1">gnyis snang &#x27;khrul pa&#x27;i bag chags</span> kyis <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w16"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s219w17">ma</span> bslad pa</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w18">zag <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s219w19">med</span></span> yin pas, de&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w20">ngo bor</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w21">bag la nyal</span> de <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w22">gnas</span> pa mi rigs la, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w23"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s219w24">dbang</span> <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s219w25">shes</span></span> kyang de&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w26">rten</span> du <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w27">med</span> cing <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w28">gzugs</span> kyang de&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w29">rten</span> du <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w30">mi rigs</span> la <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w31">kun gzhi</span> yang mi &#x27;dod pas de&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w32">rten</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w33">med</span> par &#x27;gyur ro snyam na, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w34">skyon</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w35">med</span> de <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s219w36">de&#x27;i tshe</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w37"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s219w38">nga</span> <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s219w39">tsam</span></span> zhig <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w40">sgom spang</span> gi <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w41">bag la nyal</span> gyi <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w42">rten</span> yin pa&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s219w43">phyir</span> te, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219p2"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s219w44">spang</span> <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s219w45">gnyen</span></span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w46">gzhan</span> la <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s219w47">yang</span> <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s219p3">de bzhin du shes par bya&#x27;o</span></span>
</div>
<div class="eng"><div class="lab">GESHE MICHAEL'S ENGLISH (VERBATIM)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s219S">One might wonder about something else: Let&#x27;s talk about the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w4">period</span> while you are in the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w3">&quot;uninterrupted&quot; stage</span> of the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w1">path of <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s219w2">seeing</span></span> [the actual direct perception of emptiness]. I can accept that at this point the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w5">negative thoughts</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w6">eliminated by this path</span> are <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w7">no</span> longer present, but we would have to say that the negative things <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w8">eliminated by the path of habituation</span> are still there, in a <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w9">dormant</span> way. <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s219w10">At this particular point in time</span>, the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w11"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s219w13">consciousness</span> of the <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s219w12">mind</span></span> is <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w18"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s219w19">un</span>stained</span>, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w16"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s219w17">un</span>affected</span> by the <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s219p1">mental seed which causes the mistaken state of mind where the appearance and actuality of things are different from one another</span>. As such none of these things could <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w22">lie</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w21">dormant</span> here, due to its very <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w20">quality</span> at the time. There is <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w27">no</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w23"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s219w25">consciousness</span> of the <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s219w24">senses</span></span> that could act as the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w26">basis</span> for those mental seeds, and it would be <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w30">improper</span> to say that <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w28">physical form</span> could ever provide such a <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w29">basis</span> either. According to you, moreover, there&#x27;s no <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w31">foundation consciousness</span>. I would have to think then that there is <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w33">no</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w32">basis</span> at all where these dormant things could stay. And yet there is <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w35">no</span> such <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w34">problem</span>, <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s219w43">for</span> <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s219w36">at this point in time</span> it is the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w37"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s219w39">simple</span> &quot;<span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s219w38">me</span>&quot;</span> which is providing the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w42">basis</span> for the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w41">dormant</span> things <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w40">eliminated by the path of habituation</span> to stay. You can <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s219p3">apply this reasoning</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s219w47">as well</span> to all the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219w46">other</span> cases involving <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s219p2"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s219w44">things to be eliminated</span>, and the <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s219w45">antidotes</span> which eliminate them</span>. ********* Selection Three: The Middle-Way School on the question of where the seeds of karma stay until they give their resu</span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; PROVISIONAL machine alignment reconciled by Codex from two independently replayed proposals. The complete gnyis snang 'khrul pa'i bag chags explanation is kept at phrase depth: mental seeds are the cause of the mistaken appearance/actuality disparity, not the disparity itself; no atom claims the explanatory relative clause. ILL:1873 supplies related causal wording elsewhere in the corpus, without establishing publication independence. spang gnyen is the established paired technical unit for objects of elimination and their antidotes; its two tighter members own things to be eliminated and antidotes, while the relative clause stays inside the whole compound. de bzhin du shes par bya'o retains the complete apply-this-reasoning recast at phrase depth; yang owns as well. All four basis occurrences and dormant occurrences 1, 2 and 4 are distinguished; dormant 3 is the English objection recap without a further bag la nyal. Med takes only no where a wider modal or temporal frame would overcapture. yod dgos, mi 'dod and the first mi rigs frame remain distributed and unpaired, not null. The 1500-character E-107 cap ends in resu in the appended heading; the complete main translated paragraph reaches the antidotes sentence, and no missing text is invented or refiled.</div>
